speechtext:
The House resumed consideration of the motion of Mr. Turner (Vancouver Quadra):
That this House condemns the Government for its mismanagement
of the Canadian economy, including:
1)	the threat to impose a new 9 per cent sales tax that is regressive, inequitable, invisible and inflationary;
2)	an unjustifiable high interest rate policy, with an interest rate spread between Canada and the United States that is at record highs;
3)	negligence in the management of Canadian trade causing unparallelled reductions in our trade balance and a loss of jobs, and threatening the survival of many formerly thriving Canadian industries;
4)	abondonment of Canadian primary producers with resulting undermining of the farming, fishing and forest industries; and
5)	continued neglect of regional disparities.

